I run nethack from a VT320 connected to a Unix box. The VT320 has a lot of
functions keys I could use for macros. Unfortunately, these work only in
VT320 mode, not in VT100 compatibility mode. Unfortunately, Unix does not
support my terminal in VT320 mode. In other words, I can't tie macros to
function keys, so it would have to be something like ^something-1 to execute
macro #1, etc. This is a pain to type, especially as DEC thinks the CAPS LOCK
key is much more important than the Ctrl key and should be much easier to hit,
and the bottom line is that this would not solve the typing error problem.

